            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0878" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg864"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The report of the Commission of Investigation was signed at Geneva on May 23,
                    1947, and was mimeographed by the Security Council as document S/360 four days
                    later. The conclusions and proposals (<ref target="#pg167">pages 167</ref> and
                        <ref target="#pg248">248</ref>) paralleled those contained in telegrams 299,
                    May 12, and 373, May 20, from Geneva. The sentence “On the basis of facts
                    ascertained by the Commission, it is its conclusions [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >sic</hi>] that Yugoslavia, and to a lesser extent, Albania, and Bulgaria,
                    have supported the guerrilla warfare in Greece” appears in the report on <ref
                        target="#pg167">page 167</ref>. The conclusions were subscribed to by the
                    Delegations of Australia, Belgium, <pb facs="0879" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/>
                    Brazil, China, Colombia, Syria, the United Kingdom, and the United States. The
                    Delegations of the Soviet Union and Poland did not approve the conclusions and
                    the French Delegation abstained. The United Nations has published the
                    Commission’s report in <hi rendition="#italic">Official Records of the Security
                        Council, Second Year, Special Supplement No. 2</hi>.</p>
                <p>For a summary statement of the work of the Commission and the texts of its
                    conclusions and proposals, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, July 6, 1947, pages 14–24.</p>
            </div>
